Human: Can you tell me the steps to write an if/then statement in C programming language?

Assistant: Sure, here’s how you could write an if/then statement in C:

first, you’d define a boolean variable in C and initialize it to zero.  To make the condition of your if/then statement true, you’ll set your variable to one.  Otherwise, you’ll set it to zero.  If your variable is still zero, you’re done!  If it’s not zero, your if/then statement is false, and you will execute the code inside the if clause:

example:
if(x > 5) {
  cout << "I am very glad that you wrote this statement." << endl;
}
else {
  cout << "I am very sorry, but the condition of the statement is not met." << endl;
}
